  "pattern": "sangat + word · word + sekali · word + banget (casual) · agak + word · terlalu + word",
  "explanation": "There are three ways to say 'very', and each has its place. Sangat goes before the describing word and sekali after it: sangat enak and enak sekali both mean 'really delicious'. Banget also goes after, and is the casual one, for friends: enak banget. For 'a bit' or 'rather', put agak in front: agak pedas (a bit spicy). For 'too', it's terlalu: terlalu mahal (too expensive).",
  "natural": "Enak sekali! is the safe, warm compliment for a host's cooking. Agak softens a complaint politely: Agak mahal, ya (It's a bit pricey, isn't it?).",
  "stiff": "Each word keeps its side: sekali enak and enak sangat are wrong. Banget to an older stranger sounds too casual, so use sekali there.",
